0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 22 540 [
[(Real-time audio input and output for Pd is provided by [adc~] and)]
[([dac~], respectively. "adc" stands for "Analog to Digital Converter")]
[(and "dac" stands for "Digital to Analog Converter". This gives the)]
[(idea that inputs and outputs are only analog signals, but that's)]
[(misleading as you can also have digital inputs and outputs \050it all)]
[(depends on your soundcard configuration\051. By default these objects)]
[(are stereo \050with channel numbers 1, 2\051 but you can specify different)]
[(channel numbers via arguments as in:)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 42 342 [
[(The number of channels Pd inputs and outputs also depends on)]
[(your soundcard. The soundcard and number of ins/outs are set on)]
[(Pd's command line or in the "audio settings" dialog. You can)]
[(open patches that want more channels out of range, these will be)]
[(dropped in [dac~] or output zero in [adc~].)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 53 162 [
[(If more than one [dac~] outputs to the same channel, the)]
[(signals are added. Duplicate [adc~] objects output duplicate)]
[(signals.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 311 27 [
[(updated for Pd version 0.54)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
